    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110">

                <pb facs="0225" n="199" xml:id="pg199"/>

                <head>110. Memorandum of Conversation<anchor n="0" xml:id="d110-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" type="conversation-or-meeting-date"
                            when="1958-05-23">May 23, 1958</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Indonesian Situation</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <label>PARTICIPANTS</label>
                    <item>Mr. Moekarto, Indonesian Ambassador</item>
                    <item>The Secretary</item>
                    <item>Mr. Mein, Director, Office of
                        Southwest Pacific Affairs</item>
                </list>
                <p>In a discussion of the Indonesian situation the Secretary said he wished to
                    assure the Ambassador that we are seeking to prevent acts from neighboring
                    countries designed in some form to help those who seem to be trying to stop the
                    drift of Indonesia toward communism. He said that we cannot go on exerting this
                    pressure, and he is not sure we will wish to do so, unless something is done by
                    the Indonesian Government to stop the drift. The Secretary said he hoped,
                    therefore, that the government would take such action as is possible to curb the
                    trend.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
